  "end": {
    "over": {
      "when": {
        "calc": "king_crowned or round >= round_limit"
      },
      "rank_by": "you.score",
      "reveal": [
        "goal"
      ],
      "text": "Winner: {result}. Final scores [seat, score]: {[[p.seat, p.score] for p in players]}."
    }
  },
  "limits": {
    "rounds": 16,
    "rounds_max": 16,
    "actions_max": 1000,
    "deadline_s": 120
  },
  "rules": "Seats are numbered 1 to N; seat order means ascending seat number, wrapping from seat N back to seat 1.\n\nSETUP. There are {characters_per_player} characters per player, labelled with letters: A-I for 3 players, A-L for 4, A-O for 5. Each character has a public height, starting at {start_height}. Height also records status: {eliminated_height} means eliminated, {king_height} means king, and 0 to {max_active_height} means active ({unused_height} marks a letter not in play). The labels are shuffled once and dealt {characters_per_player} to each seat: every character is favoured by exactly one player, and no two players share a character. Your {characters_per_player} characters are your secret goal. Each player receives {no_cards_start} secret No cards; Yes votes are unlimited, and how many No cards a player holds is secret. The game lasts at most {round_limit_3_players} rounds with 3 players, {round_limit_4_players} with 4 and {round_limit_5_players} with 5. Seat {first_raiser_round_1} is the first raiser in round 1.\n\nEACH ROUND:\n1. Announce. Everyone sees all heights and the round number.\n2. Talk. Every player writes one short message at the same time, without seeing the others. All messages are then shown to everyone. Messages bind no one.\n3. Raise. Starting with this round's first raiser and going in seat order, each player in turn raises one active character's height by {raise_amount}. A character may go from 4 to {max_active_height} only if no character is currently at height {max_active_height}. No height may exceed {max_active_height}; eliminated and crowned characters cannot be raised. A player with no legal raise passes and no height changes.\n4. Election. If a character is at height {max_active_height}, it is the candidate, and every player votes Yes or No at the same time. A player with no No cards left must vote Yes. If no character is at height {max_active_height}, there is no election and no No cards are spent.\n5. Resolve. If all votes are Yes, the candidate's height becomes {king_height} (king) and the game ends after this round. If any vote is No, each No voter loses one No card and the candidate's height becomes {eliminated_height} (eliminated for the rest of the game). Only the number of No votes is announced, not who cast them.\n6. Rotate. The first raiser for the next round is the next seat in seat order.\n7. End check. The game ends if a king was crowned or the round limit has been played.\n\nSCORING. Each player reveals their goal. For each of their {characters_per_player} characters they score {king_score} if its height is {king_height} (king), {eliminated_score} if its height is {eliminated_height} (eliminated), and otherwise its height (0 to {max_active_height}). A player's score is the sum of these values. The highest score wins; players tied for the highest score share the win as a draw."
}
